Package: AMDconfigurations
Type: Package
Title: Tools for AMD-Based Configuration Analysis in Complex Systems
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Manuel",
        family = "Barreiro",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "your.email@domain.com"
    )
Description: 
    Provides tools for analysing recurrent configurations in complex systems 
    using the Average Membership Deviation (AMD) framework. Includes functions 
    for estimating the optimal number of clusters, generating synthetic datasets 
    with controlled compactness, calibrating sigma-equivalent noise levels, and 
    selecting the best fuzzy c-means partition across repeated initialisations. 
    Designed to support research on geometric and energetic principles of 
    organisation across biological, ecological, geohistorical, and financial systems.
